<title>UK: Blast hits UK chemical plant, some injured.</title>
<headline>Blast hits UK chemical plant, some injured.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A number of people were injured by an explosion on Tuesday at a chemical factory just north of London, police said.</p>
<p>Police said the blast happened at Kemark Chemicals Ltd in Bletchley.</p>
<p>Police said factories and members of the public in the vicinity of the industrial estate had been evacuated as a precautionary measure.</p>
<p>Earlier reports to police said there was a large amount of smoke covering the area.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7950</p>
